<title>USA: TABLE - Tadiran Ltd Q2 net decreases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Tadiran Ltd Q2 net decreases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					 June 30		June 30</p>
<p>				     1997     1996     1997	1996</p>
<p> Sales and revenues     $ 298,716$ 311,389 $ 576,554$ 580,792</p>
<p>Gain from issuance of shares</p>
<p>  by a subsidiary		   -   33,699	   -   33,699</p>
<p>Income after income taxes</p>
<p>				   15,439   57,303    32,390   76,287</p>
<p>Equity in results of affiliates</p>
<p>					 12    (247)     (396)    (423)</p>
<p> Minority interests	 (1,398)  (4,082)   (2,431)  (4,308)</p>
<p>   Net income		  14,053   52,974    29,563   71,556</p>
<p> Earnings per share	    0.72     2.70	1.51     3.65</p>
<p> Shares outstanding	  19,614   19,614    19,614   19,614</p>
<p>		  (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income for the second quarter of 1996 included a $33.7 million gain from the initial public offering of the company's subsidiary Tadiran Telecommunications Ltd.</p>
<p>Excluding the gain, net income for the second quarter of 1996 would have been $19.3 million, or $0.98 per share.</p>
<p>Net income for the second quarter of 1997 was negatively effected by abnormal financing expenses of $9 million which were a reflection of the 6.7 percent devaluation of the New Israeli Shekel (NIS) in relation to the dollar which occurred primarily at the end of the quarter and losses on hedging transactions in respect of inflation, and a capital gain of $2 million mainly associated with the sale of a portion of Tadiran Ltd's subsidiary, Tadiran Appliances Ltd.</p>
</text>
